{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": "Keyword rules for auto-categorising imported statement rows. Matched against the row's description, counterparty and the bank's own category text. `category` is matched case-insensitively against the user's own category names; `aliases` are alternative names for the same concept, so a rule still fires when the user named the category differently. A rule whose category (and aliases) match nothing in the user's account is simply skipped. Higher `priority` wins; ties break toward the longer matched keyword. v2 targets the account's actual expense categories: Charity, Dining, Entertainment, Groceries, Health, Housing, Other, Personal Care, Remitance, Shopping, Subscription, Transport, Travel, Utilities. A category may have more than one rule when different signals deserve different priorities. The income rules are kept for accounts that add income categories later.",
